WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.580
Let's put some realistic numbers into the formula.

00:03.320 --> 00:07.840
Suppose your car has a curb-to-curb turning circle diameter of 10.8 meters,

00:08.460 --> 00:11.360
which means the radius R is 5.4 meters.

00:12.120 --> 00:18.080
Let's say the wheelbase L is 2.6 meters, the front overhang K is 1.3 meters,

00:18.400 --> 00:22.420
and the parked car in front has a width W of 1.7 meters.

00:22.980 --> 00:28.000
When we crunch those numbers, the formula tells us the parking space must be at least

00:28.000 --> 00:31.260
the length of your car plus 1.43 meters.

